      <VERS vnumber="8">We have a <gr str="6996">little </gr>
        <gr str="269">sister</gr>, and she hath no <gr str="7699">breasts</gr>: what shall we <gr str="6213">do </gr>for our <gr str="269">sister </gr>in the <gr str="3117">day </gr>when she shall be spoken <gr str="1696">for</gr>?</VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="9">If she <STYLE css="font-style:italic">is</STYLE> a <gr str="2346">wall</gr>, we will <gr str="1129">build </gr>upon her a <gr str="2918">palace </gr>of <gr str="3701">silver</gr>: and if she <STYLE css="font-style:italic">is</STYLE> a <gr str="1817">door</gr>, we will <gr str="6696">inclose </gr>her with <gr str="3871">boards </gr>of <gr str="730">cedar</gr>.</VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="10">I <STYLE css="font-style:italic">am</STYLE> a <gr str="2346">wall</gr>, and my <gr str="7699">breasts </gr>like <gr str="4026">towers</gr>: then was I in his <gr str="5869">eyes </gr>as one that <gr str="4672">found </gr>
